error[E0277]: `paginate` reads this expression as a closure, and its value is `Paging<probe::Call<List>>`, which is not a closure
  --> tests/pagers/refused/matrix_label_exit_tail.rs:35:70
   |
35 |         GET list(after?: String) -> Page { query { after; } paginate 'done: { break 'done concord::by_cursor(after, tok) }; }
   |                                                                      ^^^^^ a closure is needed here
   |
   = help: the trait `for<'a> FnMut(probe::Call<List>, &'a Answer<Page>)` is not implemented for `Paging<probe::Call<List>>`
   = note: if the value is a pager, write `.into_fn()` after a `Paging<…>` (`by_cursor(…).into_fn()`) or `Paging::from_pager(…).into_fn()` around a pager of yours; or write the pager as a call or a path, alone or at each tail of a plain block, `if` or `match`
   = note: if it is not, it is neither a closure nor a pager, and `paginate` cannot use it
   = note: required for `Paging<probe::Call<List>>` to implement `concord::__private::InferredPager<probe::Call<List>, _>`
